#─── use tailscale for secure remote access: ───────────────────────────────────────

ID: sij-mbp16
IP: 100.64.64.20
SUBNET: 100.64.64.0/24
MDNS: goby-grue.ts.net
API_KEY: '{{ SECRET.TAILSCALE_API_KEY }}'
ADDRESS: 'http://{{ ID }}.{{ MDNS }}'

#─── notes: ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ID currently has two roles: it's used to assemble the complete MagicDNS of 
#      the server, and it determines what the /id endpoint on the health router returns. 
#      This is relevant where multiple servers run the script behind a load balancer 
#      (e.g. Caddy), as a means to check which server responds. 
#      Bear in mind that /id is NOT API key-protected by default here.
#
#   IP should match the Tailscale IP of the device. But this is deprecated, 
#      and if the functionality becomes relevant again, it should be come back in 
#      the form of a dynamic check (`tailscale status` in a shell subprocess) in 
#      __init__.py or even the /id endpoint.
#
#   SUBNET should match the IP/CIDR-format tailnet
#
#   MDNS should match the tailnet's MagicDNS domain
#
#   ... don't go touching API_KEY or ADDRESS though.
#
#                                   ──────────                                        